{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #9</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #14</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the square shown, the numbers in each row, column, and diagonal multiply to give the same result. The sum of the two missing numbers is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee1e5ac194e6a2f003d9a6c3d51e2d824637518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 28 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 30 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 38 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the missing numbers, like this:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr /> \n<p>From the middle row and the middle column, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/106f022b69b5c96a60479f829be40b154a32f315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 6 \\times Y = 9 \\times 6 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01b7d4779bd7683eb6b885937f4f1405ae76b769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 9 \\times 4 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>From the bottom row and middle column, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297f22ee56fab3cdf1d60185334c13d9656b108d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 9 \\times X = 1 \\times 6 \\times 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/09684df6cd42af511b1a5944b6bdc742f36408ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = \\frac{1 \\times 6 \\times 36}{12 \\times 9} = \\frac{6 \\times 9 \\times 4}{6 \\times 2 \\times 9} = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"298\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e027a224a3b2d3fe2e85f4b7921786f521ab20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X + Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, like the problem asked for, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd6631cee5f45bdcc869f5bcb65bc9a16d45da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 36 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href